        {
          "name": "comment",
          "value": "<h2>ORDER ANOMALY SCORING WORKFLOW</h2><p><strong>Purpose:</strong></p><p>Evaluate a Salesforce order using a pre-trained Isolation Forest model</p><p>and determine whether the order exhibits anomalous behavior.</p><p><strong><em>Workflow Steps</em></strong></p><p><strong>1. Fetch Order Data</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Retrieve order details from Salesforce using order_id</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Load order attributes required for anomaly detection</p><p><strong>2. Flatten &amp; Prepare Data</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Flatten nested Salesforce objects</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Convert order data into model-ready format</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Remove unsupported complex fields</p><p><strong>3. Load Trained Model</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Load previously trained Isolation Forest model</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Reuse production anomaly detection model</p><p><strong>4. Generate Anomaly Score</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Score the order using the Isolation Forest model</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Calculate anomaly metrics and mean_length score</p><p><strong>5. Classify Order</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• mean_length &gt; 0.85 → Anomalous Order</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• mean_length ≤ 0.85 → Normal Order</p><p><strong>6. Persist Results</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Save Order ID and anomaly classification</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;• Update anomaly results in MySQL database</p><p><strong><em>Outcome:</em></strong></p><p>Provides real-time anomaly detection for incoming orders and enables</p><p>risk-based review of suspicious transactions before downstream processing.</p>",
          "widget": "textarea_rich"
        }
      ],
      "engine": "scala,pyspark,polars,agent",
      "inputAnchors": [],
      "outputAnchors": [],
      "agentTool": false
    }
